-- A derived context keeps the `equatable` flag (checker-v2.md §11.2): see
-- Main.beni. `H.eq` is unannotated and compares its payloads with
-- `Basics.eq`, so its `a` is `equatable`: it asks no evidence, but it may
-- only be given a type the structural walk can compare.
--
-- (2026-10-02: `Basics.eq` and `Basics.neq` ask for `eq` through a
-- `where` clause, as `==` does — static-dispatch-spike.md §3.1, amended —
-- and no longer through the `equatable` marker. The refusal stands; it is
-- reached the way a `where` clause's is.)
pub type Holder a
    = Holder a


pub eq (Holder x) (Holder y) = Basics.eq x y
